// Title: HackTool - SOAPHound Execution
// Sigma ID: e92a4287-e072-4a40-9739-370c106bb750
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: @kostastsale
// Date: 2024-01-26 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: discovery, T1087
// Description: Detects the execution of SOAPHound, a .NET tool for collecting Active Directory data, using
//   specific command-line arguments that may indicate an attempt to extract sensitive AD
//   information.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/FalconForceTeam/SOAPHound
//   - https://medium.com/falconforce/soaphound-tool-to-collect-active-directory-data-via-adws-165aca78288c
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_soaphound_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains " --buildcache " or ProcessCommandLine contains " --bhdump " or ProcessCommandLine contains " --certdump " or ProcessCommandLine contains " --dnsdump ") and (ProcessCommandLine contains " -c " or ProcessCommandLine contains " --cachefilename " or ProcessCommandLine contains " -o " or ProcessCommandLine contains " --outputdirectory")
